{"id": "EUVD-2026-102298", "enisaUuid": "a8eda678-b015-307e-bcad-e87698f8e7fb", "description": "Web3.py 7.15.0 through 7.16.0 and 8.0.0b2 through 8.0.0 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability because _check_ip_blocked() does not unwrap IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses in CCIP Read URL validation. Malicious contracts can return OffchainLookup URLs with IPv4-mapped IPv6 hosts or AAAA records, making clients with CCIP Read enabled send requests to loopback, private, or link-local services.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:29:53", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ethereum/web3.py/pull/3875", "https://github.com/ethereum/web3.py/blob/c8c1ed0c9e77e1a8b74902e6a6825e0b00534b10/web3/utils/ccip_url_validation.py#L16-L57", "https://github.com/ethereum/web3.py/security/advisories/GHSA-5hr4-253g-cpx2", "https://github.com/ethereum/web3.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/web3-py-7.15.0-through-7.16.0-and-8.0-0b2-through-8.0.0-ccip-read-ssrf-bypass"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w8h5-xcmp-474f", "CVE-2026-111171"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac75bb3c-1de9-317f-ae44-c074f887f8ff", "product": {"name": "web3.py", "vendor": {"name": "ethereum"}}, "product_version": "7.15.0 \u22647.16.0"}, {"id": "c794a159-5724-361c-89e5-4605181a9b36", "product": {"name": "web3.py", "vendor": {"name": "ethereum"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0b2 \u22648.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3ce6934c-95bd-31c0-a9e0-3730a772e518", "vendor": {"name": "ethereum"}}], "isExploited": false}